<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma Ying-jeou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma Ying-jeou is a Taiwanese politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> who was mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taipei">Taipei</a> and president of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 2008 to 2016. He pursued closer economic ties with the People's Republic, opening direct flights and signing a trade framework agreement in 2010. In 2015 he met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xi-jinping">Xi Jinping</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, the first meeting between leaders of the two sides since 1949.</p></div>
